---
description: Run graph coverage on changes before a pull request
alwaysApply: true
---

Before opening or updating a pull request, any agent working in this repo follows the graph-coverage skill at `.cursor/skills/graph-coverage` on its changes. Read that skill for how to interpret the report; do not duplicate it here.

From the repository root (`TEMP` must be a writable directory; if it is unset, set it to `/tmp` first):

```bash
node .cursor/skills/graph-coverage/scripts/graph-coverage.mjs --summary --out "$TEMP/graph-coverage.json"
```

The analysis is static test linkage, not executed coverage.

Include the findings in the pull request description: coverage ratios, untested gaps in new or changed code, and blast radius.

Add unit tests for the gaps it finds in the new and changed code, then run the command again and confirm those gaps are closed.
